---
title: "Reusing an actor id after state loss: two writes share one name"
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant A as A
    participant B as B
    Note over A: write<br/>A:1→"x"
    A->>B: 
    Note over B: sync<br/>A:1→"x"
    Note over A: state lost<br/>∅
    Note over A: write<br/>A:1→"y"
    A->>B: 
    Note over B: sync<br/>A:1→"x"
    B->>A: 
    Note over A: sync<br/>A:1→"y"
    Note over A: both writes are dot A:1: the reborn replica reissued a name it had already used
    Note over B,A: B keeps "x" and A keeps "y": each believes it already holds the other's write, so they never converge
